        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sergio Leone, Jon Paul Puno, Lee Van Cleef\n- Roles: film director, producer, screenwriter, filmmaker, singer, actor\n- Concepts: Spaghetti Western\n- Works: For a Few Dollars More\n\nFacts:\n- Sergio Leone was born on 3 January 1929 and died on 30 April 1989.\n- Sergio Leone was an Italian film director, producer, and screenwriter.\n- Sergio Leone is credited as the inventor of the Spaghetti Western genre.\n- Jon Paul Puno was born in 1985.\n- Jon Paul Puno is an American filmmaker and classical crossover singer.\n- After Lee Van Cleef suffered serious injuries in a car crash, he began to lose interest in his apparently waning career.\n- Sergio Leone gave Lee Van Cleef a major role in For a Few Dollars More.",
